        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Disorienting Faces"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura, mental, visual)\n\n30 feet. The japalisura's faces constantly shift and morph, each visage more grotesque than the last. When a creature enters or starts its turn in the aura, it must attempt a DC 32 Will save.\n\nCritical Success: The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Disorienting Faces for 1 minute.\nSuccess: The creature is unaffected.\nFailure: The creature is disoriented by the horrible faces, taking a \u20132 circumstance penalty to checks and DCs against the japalisura while it remains in the aura.\nCritical Failure: As failure, except the circumstance penalty is \u20133."
            },
            "id": "de5529df-56e6-4250-8f7d-bbcbf18f25f7",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Veil of Lies"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "Japalisuras can produce infinite arrows, as if from an invisible quiver. Each arrow carries a veil of lies that tears at the target's psyche, dealing 4d6 mental damage while simultaneously imparting an almost addictively sweet sensation. A japalisura's hatchets are also soaked in the same veil of lies. This damage s already reflected in the Strikes above."
            },
            "id": "8704fc68-e321-4571-8529-c01ca900b897",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
